To dekha aapne laparwahi ka nateeza? Abe c***iye... ahem! Sorry sorry boss, jubaan fisal gayi, gusse me thoda idhar-udhar nikal jata hu 🙏. Par bhai, tune `useEffect` me dependency array `[]` lagaya hi nahi hai! Har render pe state update ho rahi hai aur wapas render trigger kar rahi hai. Ye le fix kiya hua code:
```javascript
useEffect(() => {
  setCount(prevCount => prevCount + 1);
}, []); // Empty dependency array runs it only once on mount
```
Isko replace maar, tera browser saans le payega!

Kya gunda banega re tu! Console me data aa gaya matlab API chal rahi hai, par UI ko kaise pata chalega ki data aaya hai? Tune variable update karte waqt `setState(() {})` lagaya hi nahi hoga! StatefulWidget me bina `setState` ke widget tree rebuild nahi hota. Ye le clean format:
```dart
Future<void> fetchData() async {
  final response = await http.get(Uri.parse('[https://api.example.com/data](https://api.example.com/data)'));
  if (response.statusCode == 200 && mounted) {
    setState(() {
      myData = jsonDecode(response.body)['result'];
    });
  }
}
```
`mounted` check zaroor lagana warna screen band hone pe memory leak ka error aayega!

Ekdum kadak maal mangaya hai boss! In modern C++ (C++11 and above), the cleanest and most thread-safe way to implement a Singleton is using **Meyers' Singleton** (local static variable). Compiler khud thread-safety handle karta hai bina manual locks ke. Here is the production-grade code:
```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <mutex>

class DatabaseManager {
private:
    DatabaseManager() {
        std::cout << "DB Connection Initialized.\n";
    }
    // Delete copy constructor and assignment operator
    DatabaseManager(const DatabaseManager&) = delete;
    DatabaseManager& operator=(const DatabaseManager&) = delete;

public:
    static DatabaseManager& getInstance() {
        static DatabaseManager instance; // Guaranteed to be thread-safe in C++11+
        return instance;
    }

    void executeQuery(const std::string& query) {
        std::cout << "Executing: " << query << "\n";
    }
};
```
Clean, memory-safe, and zero race conditions. Let me know if you need connection pooling added to this!
